{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content","id":1488988,"title":"Speculation on future 5th Edition content?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-03T10:28:56-07:00","id":1488988,"title":"Speculation on future 5th Edition content?","content":"With Vampire and Hunter 5th Edition out, and information about the changes to Werewolf already know, I was wanting to ask around; what changes do you think are going to be brought to the other game lines? Like, who would be the antagonists, who would be the future protagonists, that sort of thing? I've been hearing some speculation that the Orphans are going to be the main protagonists for Mage 5th, but again that's just speculation, so what do you guys think. <br /> <br /> I imagine that there is going to be some re-writing on Mage's stuff, so I can't say anything for that one. For Demon, I think that there is going to be greater conflict between the Demons and the Angels, with the latter taking a much bigger antagonistic role in the future. Wraith, I feel is going to be about rebelling against the rather nightmarish state of the afterlife, though who the protagonists and the antagonists are likely going to be, however, is still a mystery. Changeling is likely going to be about bringing some form of positivity to the world; however, again, I don't know who or what the exact main conflict would likely be. As for Mummy, I have no real knowledge of the game line, so I can't really offer my thoughts on the future for it in any way. <br /> <br /> Anyone have any thoughts on the matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T13:40:01-07:00","id":1489008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just Some Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content#post1488988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been hearing some speculation that the Orphans are going to be the main protagonists for Mage 5th, but again that's just speculation, so what do you guys think. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I sincerly hope this isn't true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T16:44:10-07:00","id":1489028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489008#post1489008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I sincerly hope this isn't true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im right there with you; I do fear this is going to be true however, with the Disparate crafts taking a central role.<br /> <br /> Search your feelings, you'll know it to be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T19:54:42-07:00","id":1489047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489008#post1489008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I sincerly hope this isn't true.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As much as I hope with you... given what's been shown with both V5 and H5's themes, along with what information has already been given about the changes to Werewolf for the upcoming W5, it's a very likely course for the future. There's a strong theme of rebelling against authority in general with the 5th Edition; not a bad thing in and of itself, but it's up to the devs to make the right calls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T20:20:54-07:00","id":1489050,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Based off of what we saw in Vampire and what we're seeing in Werewolf, I would predict that if we got a 5th edition Mage it would push the Orphans and Crafts into the center of the gameline. The Crafts and Orphans would set up their own alternative Crafts Council. And then you would probably see couple of Traditions leave the Tradition Council and join the Craft Council (likely Dreamspeakers and Hollow Ones).<br /> <br /> Further, I would expect the Technocracy to have any sympathetic elements get removed and go full &quot;Fascist Bad Guy&quot; status. Past that, I would not be surprised to see a Tradition join the Technocracy (maybe the Celestial Chorus in order to shove the Christian religious fundamentalists onto team &quot;Fascist Bad Guy&quot; or the Virtual Adepts because &quot;technology bad&quot;) or maybe have something like the Euthanatos go full Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Stuff like that would be in line with the sort of shakeups we've been seeing in 5e Vampire and Werewolf.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Be careful what you wish for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T20:25:03-07:00","id":1489052,"title":"","content":"I don't think that a shake up this big is happening","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T02:01:02-07:00","id":1489072,"title":"","content":"As much as I loved Demon: the Fallen and would treasure an updated edition, Demon's never coming back unless a fan writes some unofficial supplement for Storytellers Vault. Fallen Angels escaping from Hell is an end-of-the-world scenario from day one.<br /> <br /> I would be surprised to see a modern update to Wraith as well. Settling the Sixth Great Maelstrom/Avatar Storm down so that the setting is survivable again would massively disrupt the limitations on umbral adventures that Mage and Werewolf have taken for granted since the dawn of Revised Edition. It's been my understanding that the developers want to limit dimensional shenanigans even further in W5 in order to ground the game more in the real world or somesuch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T03:25:29-07:00","id":1489080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489072#post1489072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I loved Demon: the Fallen and would treasure an updated edition, Demon's never coming back unless a fan writes some unofficial supplement for Storytellers Vault. Fallen Angels escaping from Hell is an end-of-the-world scenario from day one.<br /> <br /> I would be surprised to see a modern update to Wraith as well. Settling the Sixth Great Maelstrom/Avatar Storm down so that the setting is survivable again would massively disrupt the limitations on umbral adventures that Mage and Werewolf have taken for granted since the dawn of Revised Edition. It's been my understanding that the developers want to limit dimensional shenanigans even further in W5 in order to ground the game more in the real world or somesuch.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;limitations on umbral adventures in Werewolf&quot;. Have you played Revised? The Avatar Storm doesn't exists there and the Werewolves don't care. There's quite a few umbral supplements, an adventure taking part in the cosmic umbra, an adventure taking part in the memory umbra, and a whole pathway through the Egyptian Umbra. Umbra is quite fine in Werewolf Revised. What it's going to be in W5 is a whole other kettle of fish.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T04:24:23-07:00","id":1489089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489052#post1489052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that a shake up this big is happening</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope you're right. One of the things I loved about Mage is the focus on the Traditions and Technocracy, and how neither side was all bad. If the setting continues down the road that's already been established by V5 and H5, and is already confirmed for W5, then it certainly makes some sense that there would be some BIG shake-ups for M5 as well. The focus on smaller groups like Orphans and Disparate crafts does make a little sense for M5; the focus on thin-bloods for V5 and independent hunters for H5 pretty well indicates that the similar groups in Mage would be focused as well. <br /> <br /> As for the other splats; there's already been some talk about Demon and Wraith here. I agree with Reasor; there's really no way they can update Demon at this point, since there really doesn't need to be any kind of update. If anything, a potential D5 might end up re-writing a few things to play up the conflict between Angels and Demons, but I think the game is pretty well self-contained. Wraith has a potential update; given the presence of Renegades, I could see a potential Wraith story focusing on their attempts at overthrowing the Hierarchy in the Shadowlands, which could make for a potentially interesting plotline. <br /> <br /> There hasn't been any talk about Changeling or Mummy, I noticed. I really don't know anything about the latter, but Changeling's overall story seems to be about providing some sort of positivity to the world, so I could see it work; that being said, I'm more than a little rusty on that line, so take what I've said with a grain of salt. That, and given how H5 was basically the CofD Hunter, I could see the same thing happening to Changeling. Again, that's just speculation.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what Mummy 5th would look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T10:32:12-07:00","id":1489132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489050#post1489050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Based off of what we saw in Vampire and what we're seeing in Werewolf, I would predict that if we got a 5th edition Mage it would push the Orphans and Crafts into the center of the gameline. The Crafts and Orphans would set up their own alternative Crafts Council. And then you would probably see couple of Traditions leave the Tradition Council and join the Craft Council (likely Dreamspeakers and Hollow Ones).<br /> <br /> Further, I would expect the Technocracy to have any sympathetic elements get removed and go full &amp;quot;Fascist Bad Guy&amp;quot; status. Past that, I would not be surprised to see a Tradition join the Technocracy (maybe the Celestial Chorus in order to shove the Christian religious fundamentalists onto team &amp;quot;Fascist Bad Guy&amp;quot; or the Virtual Adepts because &amp;quot;technology bad&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> or maybe have something like the Euthanatos go full Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Stuff like that would be in line with the sort of shakeups we've been seeing in 5e Vampire and Werewolf.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Be careful what you wish for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely everything you said. And the Technocracy, instead of being &quot;50 shades of gray&quot; (urgh, ok, sorry for the awful pun), they'll become cartoonish villains a la Dr. Robotinik from Sonic. Again.<br /> <br /> I have no expectations for M5, and despite that I believe I'll still end up disappointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T10:40:19-07:00","id":1489133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just Some Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489089#post1489089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I hope you're right. One of the things I loved about Mage is the focus on the Traditions and Technocracy, and how neither side was all bad. If the setting continues down the road that's already been established by V5 and H5, and is already confirmed for W5, then it certainly makes some sense that there would be some BIG shake-ups for M5 as well. The focus on smaller groups like Orphans and Disparate crafts does make a little sense for M5; the focus on thin-bloods for V5 and independent hunters for H5 pretty well indicates that the similar groups in Mage would be focused as well. <br /> <br /> As for the other splats; there's already been some talk about Demon and Wraith here. I agree with Reasor; there's really no way they can update Demon at this point, since there really doesn't need to be any kind of update. If anything, a potential D5 might end up re-writing a few things to play up the conflict between Angels and Demons, but I think the game is pretty well self-contained. Wraith has a potential update; given the presence of Renegades, I could see a potential Wraith story focusing on their attempts at overthrowing the Hierarchy in the Shadowlands, which could make for a potentially interesting plotline. <br /> <br /> There hasn't been any talk about Changeling or Mummy, I noticed. I really don't know anything about the latter, but Changeling's overall story seems to be about providing some sort of positivity to the world, so I could see it work; that being said, I'm more than a little rusty on that line, so take what I've said with a grain of salt. That, and given how H5 was basically the CofD Hunter, I could see the same thing happening to Changeling. Again, that's just speculation.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what Mummy 5th would look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Mummy, I would like the game to move away entirely from the whole fight against the Setites, and become a proper game on it's own. Fully add the Andean and Chinese mummies, sort as their &quot;clan/tribe/kith&quot; thing and finally divorcing it from just being a supplement for VtM. Let the Mummies fight the forces of Oblivion in the Underworld, fight the &quot;Spawns of Apophis&quot; or &quot;Rakshasa Demons&quot; or somesuch, anything that makes it to be their own niche, instead of being just a footnote on another game.<br /> <br /> But do not trust to hope. It has long forsaken these lands.<br /> (Elrond, The Lord of the Rings, The Two Towers)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T14:30:04-07:00","id":1489155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489132#post1489132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely everything you said. And the Technocracy, instead of being &quot;50 shades of gray&quot; (urgh, ok, sorry for the awful pun), they'll become cartoonish villains a la Dr. Robotinik from Sonic. Again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weekday syndication Sonic or Saturday AM Sonic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T18:55:42-07:00","id":1489178,"title":"","content":"Mage 5th edition really can be something else.<br /> There are many ways to go, but honestly I'm more interested in the game mechanics. Of which 4th edition's really left me kinda disappointed. <br /> But yeah, definitely they will focus on a specific group. 5th edition is going much more local, and while vampire sects are pretty much a reproductible model to put in a city, the Traditions, Alliance, Technocrats... they are each unique, and have singular groups in them. Much harder to wash then a Clan. I'm interest to see how it will go.<br /> <br /> I love Demon, Changeling, Wraith... And would be quite amazed to see them in the new edition's light. But who knows if and when we will get these...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T17:57:15-07:00","id":1489694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489052#post1489052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that a shake up this big is happening</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *Looks at H5 and what we know of W5 so far.*<br /> <br /> Yeah.....about that....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T20:22:50-07:00","id":1489710,"title":"","content":"I'd love a Demon 5, the 5th edition treatment would do it good, it has some good stuff but it needs <b>a lot </b>of changes. And I really don't see why they'd play up the Angel conflict, it makes no sense with how more grounded things tend to be in 5th. Wrait c","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T17:03:34-07:00","id":1489814,"title":"","content":"As for Mage, I'd surely keep the &quot;grey&quot; Technocracy, and work on a new divide: taking a cue from W5, as Gaia is dying, Mages know the world is metaphisycally fucked. There may be factions who want to stabilize a new Consensus, and somewhat heal the world, and others who think Earth is a sinking ship, and want to create their own pocket realms. Between these two factions, that may well cut lines across old Traditions and Convention, looms the threat of Nephandi and Crafts and Orphans fight to protect their communities and neighborhoods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T09:41:45-07:00","id":1489894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489052#post1489052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that a shake up this big is happening</div> </div> </div> </div>...and I spent weeks telling people an invasion of Ukraine wouldn't happen because by no metric would it be a good idea. Just because something is laughably wrong from a strategic point of view doesn't mean people who should know better won't do it. Vampire has been changed massively, in my opinion for the worse. Werewolf is looking to change massively, and again almost everything I've heard is ominous from my point of view. Lightning can strike as many times as it wants to, and just because something obviously isn't working doesn't mean it'll stop. Precedent says that if we get M5, it'll wildly differ from the Mage we know. But I don't even know if we'll get that far: Werewolf is too scandalous a product in this day and age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T10:00:31-07:00","id":1489897,"title":"","content":"You guys think that the Order of Hermes will get &quot;the treatment&quot;? You know, the OoH doesn't have a good record from back in the day dealing with what ended up as the Dreamspeakers, (among other stuff). So will they get the Get of Fenris treatment from some players and in the books for their past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T10:24:11-07:00","id":1489898,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As to what I'd like, this seems ok:</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489814#post1489814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Mage, I'd surely keep the &quot;grey&quot; Technocracy, and work on a new divide: taking a cue from W5, as Gaia is dying, Mages know the world is metaphisycally fucked. There may be factions who want to stabilize a new Consensus, and somewhat heal the world, and others who think Earth is a sinking ship, and want to create their own pocket realms. Between these two factions, that may well cut lines across old Traditions and Convention, looms the threat of Nephandi and Crafts and Orphans fight to protect their communities and neighborhoods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Minus Crafts and Orphans. And Technocrats and Traditions still fight each other. It's an uneasy and begrudging truce","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T10:35:53-07:00","id":1489900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489897#post1489897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys think that the Order of Hermes will get &quot;the treatment&quot;? You know, the OoH doesn't have a good record from back in the day dealing with what ended up as the Dreamspeakers, (among other stuff). So will they get the Get of Fenris treatment from some players and in the books for their past?</div> </div> </div> </div>The annoying part of that is that if you just look at philosophy, the OoH are really open minded, and politically, they are the people with moderate ideas and are thus the guys that do well to serve as an intermediary between factions that would despise one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T11:48:12-07:00","id":1489906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489900#post1489900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The annoying part of that is that if you just look at philosophy, the OoH are really open minded, and politically, they are the people with moderate ideas and are thus the guys that do well to serve as an intermediary between factions that would despise one another.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">When you say &quot;look at philosophy&quot; I don't know if you men real life Hermetism or OoH Bonisagus Hermetism, but it doesn't matter. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The thing is </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(and to be fair, they </span></span></span><i>were</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> hypocrites and biased during the Grand Convocation) they acted shitty toward natives back then and I'm just hoping they don't get written just based on that.<br /> <br /> Like the Get of Fenris who got rid of that certain camp years ago and still...<br /> <br /> BTW, and now that I think of it, is Get of Fenris falling being attributed to their past speculation? Or has anything been said?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T12:15:02-07:00","id":1489910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489906#post1489906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">When you say &amp;quot;look at philosophy&amp;quot; I don't know if you men real life Hermetism or OoH Bonisagus Hermetism, but it doesn't matter. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The thing is </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">(and to be fair, they </span></span></span><i>were</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> hypocrites and biased during the Grand Convocation) they acted shitty toward natives back then and I'm just hoping they don't get written just based on that.<br /> <br /> Like the Get of Fenris who got rid of that certain camp years ago and still...<br /> <br /> BTW, and now that I think of it, is Get of Fenris falling being attributed to their past speculation? Or has anything been said?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You can be damn sure that the M5 will be 109% about &quot;punch the nazi&quot;, all because we are living this great cultural zeitgeist upon which everything is opressive, a cultural trait born from a generation that believes that mom and daddy are opressive. So you can be absolutely sure that the OoH will be the &quot;evil fascists&quot; of the Traditions, and the Crafts are thus the only true heroes. Oh yes, and the Technocracy will just become a silly version of the SS with zero depht or motivations at all.<br /> <br /> Im sorry, but this has to be said. That's the direction that this 5e line is taking, which is to take real world politics and try to shove down the throats of players in a fictious story of a game that were supposed to be a hobbie - but nope! If you dont follow the current thing to the letter, you're an evil opressor. And that's sadly the truth for the 5e line. Even if something happened over 500 years ago for a group, doesnt matter. It doesnt matter if the OoH are perhaps the most open minded group today - they did something bad 500 years ago - KILL THE FASCISTS!<br /> <br /> And instead of WoD being a morally complex setting with profound gray morality, it will become the most idiotic cartoonish black and white heroes vs villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T12:17:40-07:00","id":1489911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489894#post1489894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and I spent weeks telling people an invasion of Ukraine wouldn't happen because by no metric would it be a good idea. Just because something is laughably wrong from a strategic point of view doesn't mean people who should know better won't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel ya brother. I too told everybody &quot;look, Putin wont do that, it would literally be the most idiotic thing he could ever do, it would literally ruin Russia in every possible way&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, just because something is absolutely dumb doesnt mean that there arent people sttuborn and dumb enough to not do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T12:37:20-07:00","id":1489912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489910#post1489910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im sorry, but this has to be said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know what you are apologizing for if that's how you feel...<br /> <br /> I hear ya, I know there's that worry about these games still going about.<br /> <br /> So, about my question: <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> is Get of Fenris falling being attributed to their past speculation? Or has anything been said?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T13:25:54-07:00","id":1489920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489910#post1489910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can be damn sure that the M5 will be 109% about &quot;punch the nazi&quot;, all because we are living this great cultural zeitgeist upon which everything is opressive, a cultural trait born from a generation that believes that mom and daddy are opressive. So you can be absolutely sure that the OoH will be the &quot;evil fascists&quot; of the Traditions, and the Crafts are thus the only true heroes. Oh yes, and the Technocracy will just become a silly version of the SS with zero depht or motivations at all.<br /> <br /> Im sorry, but this has to be said. That's the direction that this 5e line is taking, which is to take real world politics and try to shove down the throats of players in a fictious story of a game that were supposed to be a hobbie - but nope! If you dont follow the current thing to the letter, you're an evil opressor. And that's sadly the truth for the 5e line. Even if something happened over 500 years ago for a group, doesnt matter. It doesnt matter if the OoH are perhaps the most open minded group today - they did something bad 500 years ago - KILL THE FASCISTS!<br /> <br /> And instead of WoD being a morally complex setting with profound gray morality, it will become the most idiotic cartoonish black and white heroes vs villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is all this because 5th has a &quot;fascists aren't welcome&quot; disclaimer? Or because the fascist groups are no longer officially supported as playable?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T13:41:02-07:00","id":1489924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489920#post1489920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is all this because 5th has a &quot;fascists aren't welcome&quot; disclaimer? Or because the fascist groups are no longer officially supported as playable?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's because it's shallow and childish. Even the real world nazis (and Im not talking about half a dozen clowns today that make cosplay of SS buffons) had their reasoning - which, if the purpose is to TRULY avoid the same evils from happening again, should be understood at their root causes, not dilluted to the point of it becoming meaninless.<br /> <br /> In fact, by just claiming that everything is &quot;fascism&quot; is exactly how you end up enabling bad ideas to flourish, instead of attacking the roots of them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: do not think that I dont notice your passive-agressive attempt to subtle call me a fascist. You just illustrated my point by doing so. What you did was to try to imply that &quot;since Im mad that fascists are not welcomed, Im must be a fascist&quot;. The irony is that you dont realize how authoritarian it is to use <i>reductio ad hitlerum</i> (essentially, calling someone &quot;a fascist&quot;) in an argument just because the other person doesnt agree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 08-12-2022, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:14:29-07:00","id":1489936,"title":"","content":"In essence, not only would I prefer a complex Technocratic Union over just some silly Dr Robotinik, but the same holds true even for the Nefandi for example. The Nefandi being evil for the sake of evil is silly, and they are much more interesting when they are evil due to some special reasoning (even if it's a twisted reasoning). Turning technocrats into moustache twisting villains just make the entire setting a lot poorer for no good reason.<br /> <br /> For instance, there have been many works on psychology done after WW2 about the nature of evil.<br /> <br /> Now, the nazis were a bunch of nutjobs lunatics. They followed a pseudoscientific doctrine of the 19th century called &quot;Teosophy&quot;, which were some of the most idiotic bullshit ever created that mixed Social Darwinism and 19th century mysticism.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's true, nazism was a RELIGIOUS CULT, something that very few people today know. Give it a Google about what Teosophy is - among the many nonsense about it, it said that there are 8 or 7 stages of &quot;evolution&quot; of humans, amongst which there were GIANTS - yes, Im not making that up, Google it if you dont believe me (I too was shocked when I found out how much more stupid nazism is than what everybody already think it is). The 7th stage are the &quot;Aryans&quot; (aha! This is the origin of this nonsense!), which is the evolutionary stage that creates civilizations, but the 6th stage of evolution would be a sort of &quot;degenerates&quot;, who are incapable of creating generations.<br /> <br /> Hitler &quot;theology&quot; is that Aryans (the &quot;evolved&quot; people) create civilizations and conquer the &quot;uncivilized&quot; populations at the 6th stage, enslave them, and over time start to breed with their slaves, &quot;diluting the blood&quot; - and according to those idiots, that's what cause civilizations to collapse.<br /> <br /> So, jews and gypsies didnt have a nation... So, are all the pieces falling in place now? Because they didnt have a nation or &quot;civilization&quot;, they were at the 6th stage of &quot;evolution&quot; (according to the idiotic nonsense that is Teosophy), and THAT'S WHY HITLER WANTED TO KEEP THE &quot;BLOOD PURE&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, all of this bullshittery is just a bunch of idiotic nonsense, and most of the nazis were indeed evil cultist members.<br /> <br /> That's NOT however what cause psychologists to get utterly disgusted.<br /> <br /> In fact, it would be far easier to just say that the nazis were simply a bunch of lunatic madmen. This would make it far easier.<br /> <br /> Here enters a guy called Adolf Eichmann. He were a bureocrat responsible for the logistics of the death camps, who escaped to Argentina and was captured and kidnaped to be judged in Israel in the 1960's.<br /> <br /> The thing about this guy is that he WAS NOT A NAZI. There is, he didnt believe in none of the nonsense of Teosophy. He didnt care. And yet, he still sent millions to their deaths.<br /> <br /> This is what caused psychologists to get truly disgusted, by what they called &quot;banality of evil&quot;. This guy was NOT a madman or lunatic. He were a common person, just like you guys or me, and that still perpetrated untold acts of evil in the most banal way.<br /> <br /> THIS is why I say that it's important to understand the roots of evil, instead of just painting everything we dont like or dont agree with as a cartoonish depiction of a boogieman dressed in a black SS uniform and marching like a duck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T14:32:39-07:00","id":1489943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489920#post1489920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is all this because 5th has a &quot;fascists aren't welcome&quot; disclaimer?</div> </div> </div> </div>This was pretty tragic and self defeating behaviour. They're just validating the right-wing belief that the PC crowd are policing everything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or because the fascist groups are no longer officially supported as playable? </div> </div> </div>Again, self defeating behaviour. I think it more painful that existing groups are flanderized to match real world ideas. IE if the Anarchs are liberal, the Camarilla has to be conservative because they're the enemy, and to be conservative they need to be more religious/take the Lasombra/ Be a complete joke of moustache twirling villainy, despite having being very explicitly against vampire religion. V5 feels like 2016 USA when it comes to politics, it doesn't make sense with any other context.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T15:48:56-07:00","id":1489962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489943#post1489943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was pretty tragic and self defeating behaviour. They're just validating the right-wing belief that the PC crowd are policing everything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Again, self defeating behaviour. I think it more painful that existing groups are flanderized to match real world ideas. IE if the Anarchs are liberal, the Camarilla has to be conservative because they're the enemy, and to be conservative they need to be more religious/take the Lasombra/ Be a complete joke of moustache twirling villainy, despite having being very explicitly against vampire religion. V5 feels like 2016 USA when it comes to politics, it doesn't make sense with any other context.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. We already have to deal with that idiotic nonsense of right vs left in every freaking thing nowadays, I would like to have a tiny piece of peace in my moments of leisure without all the constant &quot;fascists vs commies&quot; childish dualism in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T15:59:05-07:00","id":1489966,"title":"","content":"So what about D:TF? That's a game I never got to play but I loved reading the books.<br /> <br /> I found the powers (lore) underwhelming, but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> I remember some people criticizing for its connection with Wraith and a &quot;perceived correct account of creation&quot; or something like that. And being more like The Prophecy than actual demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T16:28:21-07:00","id":1489972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489912#post1489912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, about my question: <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> is Get of Fenris falling being attributed to their past speculation? Or has anything been said?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>They're out as a playable group and are a part of a new faction consumed by something called &quot;Haglust&quot; (not sure if the spelling is correct) that are essentially extremist werewolves on steroids.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T20:09:49-07:00","id":1489990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489943#post1489943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Again, self defeating behaviour. I think it more painful that existing groups are flanderized to match real world ideas. IE if the Anarchs are liberal, the Camarilla has to be conservative because they're the enemy, and to be conservative they need to be more religious/take the Lasombra/ Be a complete joke of moustache twirling villainy, despite having being very explicitly against vampire religion. V5 feels like 2016 USA when it comes to politics, it doesn't make sense with any other context.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree, but I don't know that that necessarily holds up in the religious aspect at least. While the Camarilla did have the Lasombra join, and the Lasombra do have some Catholic church ties, and the Camarilla is now okay with Blood Cults, at the same time the Anarchs had the Ministry/Followers of Set join and those guys are by far the most super-religious faction in the game. The Ministry/Followers are also the biggest moustache twirling villains of the World of Darkness. Pentex is more cartoony and meme-y moustache twirling villains, but the Followers of Set bleed into almost every WoD gameline in a way no other group really does.<br /> <br /> As the Anarchs only have 3 major clans (Brujah, Gangrel and Ministry/Followers) it's likely that religious trappings will end up being a bigger deal in the Anarchs than it will be in the Camarilla where the Lasombra will be in the very tiny minority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T00:44:01-07:00","id":1490003,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the <i>V5 core and his writers were heavily attacked for being &quot;crypto-fascists&quot;</i> because in the Clan writeup they mentioned the possibility of a Brujah PC being an Alt-Righter (of course, earlier Clan writeups had always included the eventual skinhead Brujah), and because in dice-rolling examples someone found a 1-4-8-8 dice combination and took it as a dogwhistle.<br /> <br /> Martin Ericsson was also <i>personally accused of being a Nazi</i> based on a manipulation of its words (he said that approximately a quarter of Swedes were voting a far-right party, so when describing the world he couldn't pretend they didn't exist, and this was taken as a sign he was marketing to the far right), despite he being a member of Antifa groups in Stockholm.<br /> <br /> Even before publishing anything WOD 5e-proper, they were accused of pandering to the far right because they wanted to insert into Werewolf tribes some real-world prejudices and behaviour, and the reaction of the fanbase was extremely negative, because they felt minorities shouldn't face prejudice also in fictional products (another section of the fanbase, of course, now is accusing them of taking all the nuance out to cater to politically correctness).<br /> <br /> <i>So no one is saying that you shall not dare speak of evil (even in the appendix on Fascism), and it's not like V5 is into SJW politics (or Alt-Right politics): it's just that the game is taking a political stance.</i><br /> <br /> WOD always took political stances, and it has always been unabashedly progressive. The problem is, nowadays the political polarization is 1000% stronger compared to the early 90s, when everyone thought History had ended, so <b>when you try to take a stance, you easily take fire from both sides, and this is what unfortunately happening to WOD. </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T01:50:36-07:00","id":1490007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Holy cow...<br /> <br /> Why just not making something new? &quot;The evil Nazbols Nephandic-Spectres&quot; or something? I mean, there are already plenty of groups that are already pure, truly evil with not an ounce of grey to it, why on Earth do the writters think that turning THE FREAKING WORLD OF <b>DARKNESS</b> into a silly black and white parody is a massive improvement to the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the discussion about Werewolf in other spaces is quite nasty. There is a strong stream of people that see it as a religious fascist game promoting genocide, racial purity and amoral monsters as protagonists. Get get it especially bad due to the fact a faction of them supported the Nazi regime and continued as secret (albeit villanious) camp into the 90s. It doesn't matter that their creed was against what the Get believe, or that they were pretty much all killed in '96- '97, because the information about them being horrible is the only thing some people have heard about Werewolf.<br /> <br /> A lot of those folks never really read werewolf but they did see someone complaining about certain elements and ralied against it, amplified it in a classic game of broken telephone and created a rather negative view of the game. They never bothered to actually try and see what the game was saying about any of the things they claim it endorses. I find it ironic that I used to find the label &quot;games for mature minds&quot; a cheap publicity crack to make people buying WoD feel superior to the &quot;D&amp;D Crowd&quot;. Now I'm literally seeing people completely unable to differentiate between a history of fuckups that needs to be overcome and endorsement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T07:22:51-07:00","id":1490023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490003#post1490003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WOD always took political stances, and it has always been unabashedly progressive. The problem is, nowadays the political polarization is 1000% stronger compared to the early 90s, when everyone thought History had ended, so <b>when you try to take a stance, you easily take fire from both sides, and this is what unfortunately happening to WOD. </b></div> </div> </div> </div>If you ignore the rabbid racism of the early books, yes, the WoD very obviously leans left. Hell most popular entertainment has leaned left. However I'd argue that the issue isn't the current political polarization, though I do think that is taking it's toll. The main point of concern is how the message is delivered. Things like Star Trek Discovery or the DAV20 chapter on Ahrimanes seem more like a right wing parody of what they think lefties believe in than an actual progressive push, and it doesn't help that critical reviews offer undeserving praise to bad but politically favourable titles while negative receptions are attributed to sexist/racist trolls trying to review bomb. <br /> <br /> The first edition of Vampire was very political. But it did so with cunning and guile, and came across as something without a significant bias. If you were a lefty, great. If you were to the right? Come and play and maybe we'll change your mind. The setting was a reflection of our reality. the organizations within were organic and worked for the setting. It didn't tell you what to think, but it encouraged you to think. <br /> <br /> V5? Throw that all out the window. Lefty? Welcome. Righty? We explictly want you to put down the book and go away. More to the Center? Can't have that. The setting isn't a reflection of reality, it's a reflection of someone's wishful thinking. The Organizations within the setting aren't organic and aren't built for the setting, they're built to lampoon the later part of last decade's politics. Anarchs VS Cam= Democrats Vs Republicans. Ministry Vs Church=Democrats Vs Republicans. Sabbat? They're the most extreme right, you're not allowed to play them. Much less cerebral, much more &quot;get on the bandwagon&quot;. <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not that we've changed. It's the media that's changed. Vampire has changed. IMO, for the worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T07:49:52-07:00","id":1490026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490023#post1490023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ignore the rabbid racism of the early books, yes, the WoD very obviously leans left. Hell most popular entertainment has leaned left. However I'd argue that the issue isn't the current political polarization, though I do think that is taking it's toll. The main point of concern is how the message is delivered. Things like Star Trek Discovery or the DAV20 chapter on Ahrimanes seem more like a right wing parody of what they think lefties believe in than an actual progressive push, and it doesn't help that critical reviews offer undeserving praise to bad but politically favourable titles while negative receptions are attributed to sexist/racist trolls trying to review bomb.<br /> <br /> The first edition of Vampire was very political. But it did so with cunning and guile, and came across as something without a significant bias. If you were a lefty, great. If you were to the right? Come and play and maybe we'll change your mind. The setting was a reflection of our reality. the organizations within were organic and worked for the setting. It didn't tell you what to think, but it encouraged you to think.<br /> <br /> V5? Throw that all out the window. Lefty? Welcome. Righty? We explictly want you to put down the book and go away. More to the Center? Can't have that. The setting isn't a reflection of reality, it's a reflection of someone's wishful thinking. The Organizations within the setting aren't organic and aren't built for the setting, they're built to lampoon the later part of last decade's politics. Anarchs VS Cam= Democrats Vs Republicans. Ministry Vs Church=Democrats Vs Republicans. Sabbat? They're the most extreme right, you're not allowed to play them. Much less cerebral, much more &quot;get on the bandwagon&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's not that we've changed. It's the media that's changed. Vampire has changed. IMO, for the worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because for the most part, back in the day books/movies/episodes/game would present a philosophical/religious/political/ethical problem and the characters dealt with it in-universe depending on each characters' beliefs (sometimes having characters at both sides of the argument), leaving the audience to think about said problem for themselves and come to their own conclusions.<br /> <br /> Now? There is a lot of media that takes a particular stance on a subject and treats it like they're the ones that are right, hence people talking how (insert entertainment here) is moralizing or has an agenda.<br /> <br /> I like nuance and also I don't think I'm dumb. Present whatever dilemma you want to address and let me think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","user":"HeavyWhiskey","date":". 08-13-2022, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T17:35:23-07:00","id":1490079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all... RPGs are escapism. It's a hobby, entertainement for the purpose of having fun. In WoD, we play with INHUMAN MONSTERS with ALIEN MINDS. And in the process, we explore the concepts of morality and humanity. It's not a game for black and white Justice League paladins of virtue.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, nothing has indicated that any change will push any of our familiar monsters to an extreme of what humanity considers the paragon of heroism. We're still basically getting Shuma-Gorath's ending for Ultimate MvC 3 for most of the monsters in the setting. &quot;I saved the world? Whoops. Well, might as well roll with it...&quot;<br /> <br /> Secondly, if you go through the full extent of Uncle Gary's Fundamentalist Dogma... paladins in D&amp;D could arguably end up as worse monsters than a lot of Garou, or possibly even vampires, as Gygax was all about swordpoint conversions of orcs with summary executions to make sure that they &quot;remained saved&quot;, without any compromise to the paladins' status as LG in alignment. And all of that, wrapped up in the language of Col. John Milton Chivington, perpetrator of the Sand Creek Massacre of the Cheyenne people. A massacre so extreme that the Army of the time - a tool for steady and merciless genocide - actually condemned the action. Gygax thought he was unambiguously great, and bent over backwards to form an apologia of his actions, and his feelings had long since filtered down to (A)D&amp;D and shaped it over the course of, by the time he made the cheerleading post in the early 21st century, three decades and change.<br /> <br /> One person's entertainment, too, can appear markedly different to others. Some D&amp;D players want to kill orcs and don't bat an eye at the coding that surrounds this interaction. Others are keen on a much more compassionate standard for LG, and/or are trying to pull more of a pulp swords and sorcery experience out of the mix, a genre well known for being morally ambiguous and offering no absolutes on what happens. Is a campaign of total revenge on the thief's guild justified? Perhaps, perhaps there are ramifications that will get out of hand. But Vlana and Fafrd are going to do it, damn it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, even if that were true, so what? In WoD you can literally play with fiendish alien forces of obliteration, mad monsters of pure sheer evil like Spectres for example, upon which there are absolutely NO MORALS holding them back, to the point of being suicidal in their mayhem and utter endles hate towards everything.<br /> <br /> Even if werewolves were like that (and they arent), it's still a creature that isnt human. It would be like playing the Predator (the hunter aliens from space) and complain that they are murderous eugenists, it's totally idiotic. </div> </div> </div>Garou are still related to and tied to humanity. This helps to contrast their Rage and how their world is often filled with the shocking, gore-filled violence of the splatterpunk genre, where you are never really all that safe or proof from being turned into a pile of meat, bones, and organs. So, it wouldn't be like playing the Predator; Yautja largely don't grow up among humans or wolves and don't have any points of sympathy for them or prompts to become intimately interested with either, but a homid Garou has likely not known that they were actually different until they woke up to violence (sure they were shunned as kids, but a lot of people are shunned for no reason), while those born of wolf haven't had much time to log many differences before they, too, find themselves estranged from their fellows and thrown into a war - something that they might have thought themselves free from after being able to stand up to organized human hunts for extermination, only to find out that their side isn't really doing very well and the war is asymmetric out of necessity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hehe, I was about to say exactly that. &quot;I think people should have a little bit of maturity&quot;. In particular to differentiate between real life and fantasy. </div> </div> </div>You also have to take into account when other people don't differentiate between them, and in that case, the best course is usually not to just say or do nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T18:06:45-07:00","id":1490080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1489966#post1489966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what about D:TF? That's a game I never got to play but I loved reading the books.<br /> <br /> I found the powers (lore) underwhelming, but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> I remember some people criticizing for its connection with Wraith and a &quot;perceived correct account of creation&quot; or something like that. And being more like The Prophecy than actual demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the Lores are underwhelming, some are exceedingly powerful, consistency was a huge problem. The game does need a new edition regardless due to its many rules problems, specially Lore design.<br /> <br /> Demon easily comes off as having the correct account because, different from the other lines, you're supposed to play a direct survivor of the Original War. They talk about the Dawn of Time and everything else not as a legend they heard, but as something they witnessed, and with the confidence of someone who was literally there.<br /> <br /> But the game does put it in check with the effects of Hell on their memories. At the end of the day they're spirits whose memories do not work like human memories, then got trapped for millennia in a sensory deprivation chamber, then got trusted suddenly in reality with little time and no reference for what's going on, and then put into a human body and human brain that further muddles their minds. Their memories aren't as reliable as their confidence indicates.<br /> <br /> Other than that, it has the problem of being meant as a short-lived line instead of broadly explored, but I played it and I really like it. It is possibly my favorite WoD game, and I love Vampire and Changeling. And I disagree that the game doesn't have a reason to be updated just because it came as a end-of-the-world premise. You can adapt it perfectly fine for an ongoing setting with the factions changing to account for their plans becoming more long-term.<br /> <br /> I don't think the conflict will be with Angels, although we never know with Paradox. But the Earthbound are already well positioned to check all the boxes for what they want in their antagonists. At most I think they'll take out the &quot;amoral&quot; and intricate relationships between Factions and simplify them, fully solidifying them into two warring factions and maybe a third &quot;true rebel&quot;. For now I'd say they would make the Raveners and Luciferans into competing &quot;Sabbat-like&quot; antagonists, and the others would mix into a &quot;Camarilla-like&quot; thing. Maybe they just drop them all and make new factions altogether.<br /> <br /> That if they ever do Demon. I don't know if they will because I don't know if the setting development will ever get sufficient momentum. V5 is far slower on publication than WoD used to be. The reasons are many-fold, but the result is the same. I think the next few years will either see the setting getting momentum for we to see all the lines updated or lose it completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T02:05:51-07:00","id":1490108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490080#post1490080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon easily comes off as having the correct account because, different from the other lines, you're supposed to play a direct survivor of the Original War. They talk about the Dawn of Time and everything else not as a legend they heard, but as something they witnessed, and with the confidence of someone who was literally there.<br /> <br /> But the game does put it in check with the effects of Hell on their memories. At the end of the day they're spirits whose memories do not work like human memories, then got trapped for millennia in a sensory deprivation chamber, then got trusted suddenly in reality with little time and no reference for what's going on, and then put into a human body and human brain that further muddles their minds. Their memories aren't as reliable as their confidence indicates.</div> </div> </div> </div>What always bugged me was that not only was this the baseline stance they had, the writers used it as a soapbox to actually pontificate on other lines on a level that's not covered normally, giving even more credence to their ramblings. The supplements especially made these things claim and redefine core elements of other game lines as well as human history (Hello Jesus Morningstar!). It doesn't help that a lot of people tend to belive it verbatim and use it as the explanation of the One WoD.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T05:57:31-07:00","id":1490124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490108#post1490108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What always bugged me was that not only was this the baseline stance they had, the writers used it as a soapbox to actually pontificate on other lines on a level that's not covered normally, giving even more credence to their ramblings. The supplements especially made these things claim and redefine core elements of other game lines as well as human history (Hello Jesus Morningstar!). It doesn't help that a lot of people tend to belive it verbatim and use it as the explanation of the One WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other games never really cover how the underworld was created (as far as I remember) and personally love the explanation along with knowing how the WOD started. I think it's the companion book that has the conversation between <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">a preacher </span></span></span>and a demon that explains it in more detail. It's a good read.<br /> <br /> Is it because you'd like a more open-ended or no <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">explanation at all that you don't like it? For me, I've always had a separation between canon and what we do at our table. I pick and choose what or what not to use, and even if I don't use something I still enjoy reading it.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T10:51:28-07:00","id":1490150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490124#post1490124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it because you'd like a more open-ended or no <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">explanation at all that you don't like it? For me, I've always had a separation between canon and what we do at our table. I pick and choose what or what not to use, and even if I don't use something I still enjoy reading it.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer the splats deciding what is the truth within the context of themselves, rather than some arbitrary person at the end of the show coming in an saying &quot;HA HA, YOU ARE ALL WRONG, K THX BAAAAI&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:18:16-07:00","id":1490169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490150#post1490150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I prefer the splats deciding what is the truth within the context of themselves, rather than some arbitrary person at the end of the show coming in an saying &quot;HA HA, YOU ARE ALL WRONG, K THX BAAAAI&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So no crossover splats bleeding into each other? Got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:32:35-07:00","id":1490177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490169#post1490169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So no crossover splats bleeding into each other? Got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do what you want with crossovers. You can find cool stuff between the games and use it to make things interesting. If I'm running X:Y that's the game that's correct, everyone else isn't. I object to the way White wolf treated Demon and all the other gamelines through it. You just cannot have a game line walk in and say &quot;You know all the other characters? They are deluding themselves and we know the actual deal on them, and the word of the Author corroborates it&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T13:47:58-07:00","id":1490180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490177#post1490177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do what you want with crossovers. You can find cool stuff between the games and use it to make things interesting. If I'm running X:Y that's the game that's correct, everyone else isn't. I object to the way White wolf treated Demon and all the other gamelines through it. You just cannot have a game line walk in and say &quot;You know all the other characters? They are deluding themselves and we know the actual deal on them, and the word of the Author corroborates it&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I understood. I guess I should've said &quot;no crossover explanations&quot; or &quot;no one gameline explaining the other.&quot;<br /> <br /> Although I don't get the &quot;author corroborates it&quot; part. I mean they are the authors, so what they say is what goes for canon, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","user":"HeavyWhiskey","date":". 08-14-2022, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T14:36:02-07:00","id":1490186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490180#post1490180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I don't get the &quot;author corroborates it&quot; part. I mean they are the authors, so what they say is what goes for canon, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me put it like this:<br /> Vampire says - there is weird shit in the world, we're not sure why it's there, here's some theories, be careful they may kill you<br /> Werewolf says - there is weird shit in the world, we're not sure why it's there, here' some theories, be careful they may kill you<br /> Changeling says... You get where I'm going with this?<br /> <br /> Demon actually goes and addresses game terms, religious lore, history of the different splats and their core figures of all the other splats and completely recontextualises them within demon essentially saying they are all deluding themselves because they were there first and know what it's really like. It's about how it's done.<br /> <br /> There's no canon without a body that sits down and establishes a canon, and White Wolf never really struck out any of their books - Gypsies are still technically &quot;canon&quot;. What is weird though is that Demon tried to recontextualise all other games in the last moment as something else, in a way establishing the core principles of the game as presented in DtF supplements. In a way all the other lines were handwaving their competitors while Demon was saying &quot;Let me teal you the REAL deal&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T15:37:51-07:00","id":1490190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490186#post1490186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Gypsies are still technically &quot;canon&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Man, I'm not really sure I should do this.....gypsy is an exonym for Romani people, who actually exist. L</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">ike Germany is an exonym for Deutschland.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If you meant gypsy as for the Romani...why wouldn't they be there?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If you meant the </span></span></span><i>term</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> gypsy...sure, it could do without. It's an exonym, but one based off misunderstanding who the Romani are and where they came from. It became a pejorative because it began assuming stereotypes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm pretty use that revised started using the word Romani and integrated their Indian origins.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T15:55:17-07:00","id":1490192,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27541_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27541\" data-vbnamecard=\"27541\">HeavyWhiskey</a> I mean the 1994 book. The book that says that the people in question are magically cursed to be haunted and tormented and that their blood is magical and gives them powers and proclivities to crime? White Wolf wrote that, as well as a whole bunch of other stuff that's just absurd and sometimes downright racist. That's why I'm saying that the statement of &quot;if it's written it is canon&quot; is dubious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T15:55:21-07:00","id":1490193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490186#post1490186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no canon without a body that sits down and establishes a canon, and White Wolf never really struck out any of their books&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If a group, company or single author releases stories based on an IP they own you'd assume all of it is canon unless they say otherwise. And they <i>have</i> struck books from canon, at least once that I remember: The Red Death Trilogy.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T16:03:59-07:00","id":1490194,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I mean the 1994 book. The book that says that the people in question are magically cursed to be haunted and tormented and that their blood is magical and gives them powers and proclivities to crime? White Wolf wrote that, as well as a whole bunch of other stuff that's just absurd and sometimes downright racist. That's why I'm saying that the statement of &quot;if it's written it is canon&quot; is dubious.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">OOOOHH, yeah that...that was so long ago I've forgotten about it. I hadn't even started playing in 1994. Well, I'll say that wasn't great...however I'd think that Clan Book Ravnos Revised should supersede that.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Maybe they should officially strike it though.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","user":"HeavyWhiskey","date":". 08-14-2022, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T17:24:55-07:00","id":1490202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490080#post1490080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the Lores are underwhelming, some are exceedingly powerful, consistency was a huge problem. The game does need a new edition regardless due to its many rules problems, specially Lore design.<br /> <br /> Demon easily comes off as having the correct account because, different from the other lines, you're supposed to play a direct survivor of the Original War. They talk about the Dawn of Time and everything else not as a legend they heard, but as something they witnessed, and with the confidence of someone who was literally there.<br /> <br /> But the game does put it in check with the effects of Hell on their memories. At the end of the day they're spirits whose memories do not work like human memories, then got trapped for millennia in a sensory deprivation chamber, then got trusted suddenly in reality with little time and no reference for what's going on, and then put into a human body and human brain that further muddles their minds. Their memories aren't as reliable as their confidence indicates.<br /> <br /> Other than that, it has the problem of being meant as a short-lived line instead of broadly explored, but I played it and I really like it. It is possibly my favorite WoD game, and I love Vampire and Changeling. And I disagree that the game doesn't have a reason to be updated just because it came as a end-of-the-world premise. You can adapt it perfectly fine for an ongoing setting with the factions changing to account for their plans becoming more long-term.<br /> <br /> I don't think the conflict will be with Angels, although we never know with Paradox. But the Earthbound are already well positioned to check all the boxes for what they want in their antagonists. At most I think they'll take out the &quot;amoral&quot; and intricate relationships between Factions and simplify them, fully solidifying them into two warring factions and maybe a third &quot;true rebel&quot;. For now I'd say they would make the Raveners and Luciferans into competing &quot;Sabbat-like&quot; antagonists, and the others would mix into a &quot;Camarilla-like&quot; thing. Maybe they just drop them all and make new factions altogether.<br /> <br /> That if they ever do Demon. I don't know if they will because I don't know if the setting development will ever get sufficient momentum. V5 is far slower on publication than WoD used to be. The reasons are many-fold, but the result is the same. I think the next few years will either see the setting getting momentum for we to see all the lines updated or lose it completely.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're going to have a better perspective than me since you've actually played the game, but I'd like to see something different (and maybe for Wraith also) than the usual WOD template of tiered grouping (house-faction) with a ruling body on top (courts)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T23:09:28-07:00","id":1490221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490108#post1490108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What always bugged me was that not only was this the baseline stance they had, the writers used it as a soapbox to actually pontificate on other lines on a level that's not covered normally, giving even more credence to their ramblings. The supplements especially made these things claim and redefine core elements of other game lines as well as human history (Hello Jesus Morningstar!). It doesn't help that a lot of people tend to belive it verbatim and use it as the explanation of the One WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other lines do not do that kind of pontification?<br /> <br /> Werewolf and Mage do exactly that since their inception. They go beyond just having legends about other splats to being able to explain the whole setting under their assumptions. Specially Werewolf, you can explain each and every phenomena and splat through their view and they are quick to not only offer this explanation, but also prove their point. What stops their cosmologies from making the One WoD is just that the WoD as a whole is inconsistent.<br /> <br /> Instead, I just take DtF's lore as another take. It has an overarching quality to it just because that's a narrative need of the line, very similar to what WtA already does. If you want a &quot;vanilla Demon game&quot;, then they have the ultimate answer because that's their whole theme. But if you want a One WoD, then things are off as they are with any splat, and their confidence shouldn't be taken as evidence. After all, they're spirits, not a blend of human and something (even if they have some human memories affecting them).<br /> <br /> But the later part is true, and a problem, but where does it come from? DtF came at a time when the metaplot was almost finished and even <i>Revised</i> couldn't shy from leaking references across game lines. And while fans had more than ten years of publication to make theories with WtA and MtA as basis for a One WoD, when Demon came it threw new ideas then the world went boom. So it is less the line that had the ultimate answer and more the line that had the last word just because the party was over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490202#post1490202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to have a better perspective than me since you've actually played the game, but I'd like to see something different (and maybe for Wraith also) than the usual WOD template of tiered grouping (house-faction) with a ruling body on top (courts)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you on Demon, but I don't think that's what Paradox will do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T01:32:18-07:00","id":1490230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490221#post1490221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other lines do not do that kind of pontification?<br /> <br /> Werewolf and Mage do exactly that since their inception. They go beyond just having legends about other splats to being able to explain the whole setting under their assumptions. Specially Werewolf, you can explain each and every phenomena and splat through their view and they are quick to not only offer this explanation, but also prove their point. What stops their cosmologies from making the One WoD is just that the WoD as a whole is inconsistent.<br /> <br /> Instead, I just take DtF's lore as another take. It has an overarching quality to it just because that's a narrative need of the line, very similar to what WtA already does. If you want a &quot;vanilla Demon game&quot;, then they have the ultimate answer because that's their whole theme. But if you want a One WoD, then things are off as they are with any splat, and their confidence shouldn't be taken as evidence. After all, they're spirits, not a blend of human and something (even if they have some human memories affecting them).<br /> <br /> But the later part is true, and a problem, but where does it come from? DtF came at a time when the metaplot was almost finished and even <i>Revised</i> couldn't shy from leaking references across game lines. And while fans had more than ten years of publication to make theories with WtA and MtA as basis for a One WoD, when Demon came it threw new ideas then the world went boom. So it is less the line that had the ultimate answer and more the line that had the last word just because the party was over.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a matter of style and presentation. The reason Demon as the explanation of all worked is because it was presented in a whole different manner than Mage and Werewolf. Yes, neither of those games are crossover happy, but they don't really know what happened, they don't have access to anyone who was there, and they offer multiple often contradicting takes on their own mythology. It's clear from the way it's presented in the books that while they have stories about the others, they don't really understand them and cannot agree why the world is like that. This uncertainity creates the feeling that either game might be right and that they are getting things wrong.<br /> <br /> Demon on the other hand says, you know they are all wrong, let me tell you the story, i was there when it happened. Not only does it say that in character but presents such information out of character and is rather consistant and insistant on one interpretation of what reality really is and where core figures of other mythologies are actually featured and analysed. It's a level of engagement with the other settings that others don't have and it comes with an illusion of it being correct. With it being the last line and the authors at the time saying how it's correct (usenet was so much fun :P), we were just left with a game that pees even more into the others pool.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T03:30:15-07:00","id":1490239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490221#post1490221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">being able to explain the whole setting under their assumptions. Specially Werewolf, you can explain each and every phenomena and splat through their view and they are quick to not only offer this explanation, but also prove their point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T03:33:48-07:00","id":1490240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490230#post1490230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> is rather consistant and insistant on one interpretation of what reality really is <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll re-read D:TF to see if it really insists upon itself or just giving their account like other lines do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T05:08:05-07:00","id":1490245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490240#post1490240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll re-read D:TF to see if it really insists upon itself or just giving their account like other lines do.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you're at it, take a look at Earthbound and Houses of the Fallen. Time of Judgement also has some crazy stuff in it, but guess that one can slide due to it all being mad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T09:44:37-07:00","id":1490265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490230#post1490230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a matter of style and presentation<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> With it being the last line and the authors at the time saying how it's correct (usenet was so much fun :P), we were just left with a game that pees even more into the others pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you mean and it isn't wrong, I just want to put it into context.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of style and presentation, it makes sense. It is a need of the line. As long as we know it is style and presentation, not actual ultimate truth for the WoD as a whole, it is ok. Again, because every line will put their own style and presentation above all else, and here it is about the firs rebels of Creation. But I do agree that it should also have some doubts and possibilities planted in there, and a greater effort to make it uncertain from the PoV of others.<br /> <br /> What the authors said at Usenet is a rather thorny problem, but ultimately localized and outside the game itself. It isn't good, but it isn't canon either, and fortunately <i>Gehenna</i> took a rather necessary step at stating in full that Word of God shouldn't be taken as canon just 'cause. It may be the opinion of the authors, but it isn't in the books for a reason. That doesn't make the problem go away, but helps a lot with addressing it.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, all those problems are easy to solve in the fiction, or exist completely outside of it (WoG and fan zealotry), so they are not things that keep me from enjoying the game itself. And I personally found that Demon is plenty of fun by itself or with the other lines, even if subordinated to them. I'll soon use Demons in my Changeling game, where they're originally from the Dreaming and may or may not understand that, and I'm currently using some in a Werewolf game where they're really ancient spirits, and while their spiel is the same as in DtF, it is a blend of memories from other realms out of context, fake memories due to their spiritual nature, and posturing. Because Demons are a lot about posturing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T13:18:27-07:00","id":1490535,"title":"","content":"Demon had the worst lore and practically ruined the WoD cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T14:35:52-07:00","id":1490545,"title":"","content":"To turn the complaints into useful workshopping, I've been outlining a reimagining of Demon for 5th Edition in my head. I think of lot of problems become manageable if the game were to reframe the player characters as mortals suffering from possession, instead of as the spirits doing the possessing. Doing so retains the struggle against corruption that's familiar to so many World of Darkness games, while restoring the unreliability of the narrative. <br /> <br /> Maybe Captain Howdy was really born on the second day and used to be a guardian angel before he fell in with a bad crowd and became a plague demon, or maybe he's a party of an edgy trinity that only werewolves know about, or maybe he's something else entirely. The host is never really going to know, and that uncertainty lends itself as a storytelling tool as the character and their demon try to either control one another or build a working relationship. In game terms, the demon types should fall under another archetype organization system entirely, likely modeled loosely after their intended party role as they are in Werewolf and Hunter.<br /> <br /> Faith? Out the window, and I agree with V5's developers that the newer mechanics are more interesting than giving characters an energy gas tank. Rouse checks might lend the player Torment Dice, matching the role that Hunger Dice play in V5, as calling up the demon's Lores or persuading the demon to do it risks overlapping the host's and demon's minds and letting horrible memories or inhuman drives leak into the mortal's consciousness. High torment power effects from the original D:tF could be used as suggested examples for the results of messy crits.<br /> <br /> I think this is doable. If I was willing to make the time commitment myself, I'd consider learning the ins and outs of Storytellers Vault's publishing contract and take the idea from outline to finished book myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 08-17-2022, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T15:38:24-07:00","id":1490553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490535#post1490535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon had the worst lore and practically ruined the WoD cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly; I don't think Demon was bad, it had a cosmology that served the prupose of the story it was telling, and without the other baggage I don't mind the setup. If I cared to run Demon I'd keep the cosmos as presented. I would however ignore all references to any other game lines and I would strongly be against Demon informing anyone's views about the other lines.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T06:09:07-07:00","id":1490601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490545#post1490545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To turn the complaints into useful workshopping, I've been outlining a reimagining of Demon for 5th Edition in my head. I think of lot of problems become manageable if the game were to reframe the player characters as mortals suffering from possession, instead of as the spirits doing the possessing. Doing so retains the struggle against corruption that's familiar to so many World of Darkness games, while restoring the unreliability of the narrative.<br /> <br /> Maybe Captain Howdy was really born on the second day and used to be a guardian angel before he fell in with a bad crowd and became a plague demon, or maybe he's a party of an edgy trinity that only werewolves know about, or maybe he's something else entirely. The host is never really going to know, and that uncertainty lends itself as a storytelling tool as the character and their demon try to either control one another or build a working relationship. In game terms, the demon types should fall under another archetype organization system entirely, likely modeled loosely after their intended party role as they are in Werewolf and Hunter.<br /> <br /> Faith? Out the window, and I agree with V5's developers that the newer mechanics are more interesting than giving characters an energy gas tank. Rouse checks might lend the player Torment Dice, matching the role that Hunger Dice play in V5, as calling up the demon's Lores or persuading the demon to do it risks overlapping the host's and demon's minds and letting horrible memories or inhuman drives leak into the mortal's consciousness. High torment power effects from the original D:tF could be used as suggested examples for the results of messy crits.<br /> <br /> I think this is doable. If I was willing to make the time commitment myself, I'd consider learning the ins and outs of Storytellers Vault's publishing contract and take the idea from outline to finished book myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loving it. The way I read it is basically playing Regan McNeil. So as to that, maybe avoid making demon organizations of any sort, they're just demons. I hated that from The Exorcist series, with all the demons coming together to form a &quot;Legion of Doom&quot;. Some of them could join forces, but maybe not official groups. <br /> <br /> I'd leave the faith system, even if with some differences. I'd represent the demon getting power by tormenting the people around the character and /or loved ones.<br /> <br /> And I'll agree that hunger dice could work, despite me not liking them for V5. That would be the character being tempted to do something horrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T07:42:02-07:00","id":1490609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490545#post1490545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To turn the complaints into useful workshopping, I've been outlining a reimagining of Demon for 5th Edition in my head. I think of lot of problems become manageable if the game were to reframe the player characters as mortals suffering from possession, instead of as the spirits doing the possessing. Doing so retains the struggle against corruption that's familiar to so many World of Darkness games, while restoring the unreliability of the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this kind of &quot;solution&quot; is that it disregard the actual players of the affected line. It is the same problem with ditching the Imbued in Hunter: it may have made the game more palatable to those that never enjoyed the original in the first place, but for the fans of the original it is deeply offensive and misses the point.<br /> <br /> So, you're proposing a game of Demon where the player doesn't play with anything resembling the original splat and throws the whole lore out of the window. What did you accomplish except giving the <u>term</u> &quot;Demon&quot; a lore that's palatable for a Werewolf player?<br /> <br /> Also, conceptually this already exists. It's a fomor. And bear with me, I think a better body of rules for fomors than what we have today is a perfectly fine goal, making something that makes them interesting on their own and not necessarily following Werewolf lore, but their own lore, is quite neat, and if well done it could be a main splat on its own merits.<br /> <br /> But that's not Demon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490553#post1490553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly; I don't think Demon was bad, it had a cosmology that served the prupose of the story it was telling, and without the other baggage I don't mind the setup. If I cared to run Demon I'd keep the cosmos as presented. I would however ignore all references to any other game lines and I would strongly be against Demon informing anyone's views about the other lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>What DtF needs in an eventual new edition (be it D5 or D20 or whatever) is added uncertainty. It isn't too different from the problem of VtM with tthe Book of Nod being objectively true, even if more annoying. You can add eelements to the game that don't really contradict previous lore, but does put it in perspective and adds doubt. What if they find a hidden fortress from the War filled with evidence of what happened, but this evidence points to another story entirely?<br /> <br /> It may be a clever, well made lie... but is it? What if this evidence points to an ancient Gaian war instead, or to the war of the Tuatha? What about evidence that their memories fit perfectly... in another realm in the Horizon? Are they &quot;earthly&quot; angels that fought all across Creation, or are they aliens invading another realm they think to be their own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T07:48:18-07:00","id":1490610,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Yeah, Karkost any sentence that goes, &quot;Even the Real Nazis had some points--&quot; Is something we avoid here on the forums. Posts deleted and please dont' do that again even with a lot of caveats.<br /> <br /> Also, very aggressive posting and low-key insulting to other posters so please leave the thread.</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T08:01:37-07:00","id":1490612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490609#post1490609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this kind of &quot;solution&quot; is that it disregard the actual players of the affected line. It is the same problem with ditching the Imbued in Hunter: it may have made the game more palatable to those that never enjoyed the original in the first place, but for the fans of the original it is deeply offensive and misses the point.<br /> <br /> So, you're proposing a game of Demon where the player doesn't play with anything resembling the original splat and throws the whole lore out of the window. <br /> <br /> But that's not Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think any ideas that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11599\" data-vbnamecard=\"11599\">Reasor</a> and I have presented could be implemented without eschewing established lore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T19:09:56-07:00","id":1490671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490612#post1490612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think any ideas that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11599\" data-vbnamecard=\"11599\">Reasor</a> and I have presented could be implemented without eschewing established lore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they sure could.<br /> <br /> For <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11599\" data-vbnamecard=\"11599\">Reasor</a>'s idea I would stick to fomors, but I <b>do</b> think they're very good at that! The idea of playing Fomors have been around for a long time, the concept is fantastic in itself, but the rules have always felled short of their potential, and a big part of it is the books not wanting to stir too far away from Werewolf's perceived conflict (they <b>have</b> to be Wyrm fodder, always). A game taking the concept and exploring it without such limitation would be fantastic, with no need to shit on Werewolf, and include other possible origins, types and explanations for Fomors. Including some maybe being Fallen possessions going awkwardly wrong.<br /> <br /> Your ideas could be implemented in both cases. And I only disagree with making Faith too different from what it was. The idea of power from Faith, and Demons being by necessity cult-makers is a big part of the experience of playing it. It strikes the cord of making them a predatory presence upon humanity without making them too directly evil, so you have a lot of ambiguity on their behavior, and it is a really fun style of play. Just being a jerk to get power all the time would grow old quickly. Other than that? I think your ideas are either on-spot or at least worth trying, including that Torment would work better like that than Hunger does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T23:42:17-07:00","id":1490681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490671#post1490671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, they sure could.<br /> <br /> For <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>'s idea I would stick to fomors, but I <b>do</b> think they're very good at that! The idea of playing Fomors have been around for a long time, the concept is fantastic in itself, but the rules have always felled short of their potential, and a big part of it is the books not wanting to stir too far away from Werewolf's perceived conflict (they <b>have</b> to be Wyrm fodder, always). A game taking the concept and exploring it without such limitation would be fantastic, with no need to shit on Werewolf, and include other possible origins, types and explanations for Fomors. Including some maybe being Fallen possessions going awkwardly wrong.<br /> <br /> Your ideas could be implemented in both cases. And I only disagree with making Faith too different from what it was. The idea of power from Faith, and Demons being by necessity cult-makers is a big part of the experience of playing it. It strikes the cord of making them a predatory presence upon humanity without making them too directly evil, so you have a lot of ambiguity on their behavior, and it is a really fun style of play. Just being a jerk to get power all the time would grow old quickly. Other than that? I think your ideas are either on-spot or at least worth trying, including that Torment would work better like that than Hunger does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a good solution. It's certainly something I'd pick up on the Storyteller's Vault.<br /> <br /> I think there's a balance to be had between keeping the old versions of things in stasis and then chucking them out the window to make something entirely new. The trick is to make the new version feel like the old version, and make the old kind of games possible, while also expanding, adding and clarifying as necessary.<br /> <br /> E.g. , if you've read the new KotE stuff from hsienfan (there's a 'historical setting' for the 1990s being developed on RPG.net right now), you'll see how a game can feel new and far less problematic, while also feeling like Kindred of the East.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T04:07:43-07:00","id":1490695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490671#post1490671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">making Faith too different from what it was. Just being a jerk to get power all the time would grow old quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea would have been that torment <i>forces</i> you to be evil acts which turns to faith/power. Your possessed character would be more powerful but your life would get increasingly fucked up. But reading your post made me think that would <i>maybe</i> be putting too much trust in the players to act as against the possession, which is the core of the idea.<br /> <br /> Kinda like Wraith in a way...I guess? where your supposed to trust somebody playing your shadow. I've always read that's something some people never liked...<br /> <br /> Love your idea of formor being an umbrella term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T00:01:19-07:00","id":1490768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490695#post1490695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea would have been that torment <i>forces</i> you to be evil acts which turns to faith/power. Your possessed character would be more powerful but your life would get increasingly fucked up. But reading your post made me think that would <i>maybe</i> be putting too much trust in the players to act as against the possession, which is the core of the idea.<br /> <br /> Kinda like Wraith in a way...I guess? where your supposed to trust somebody playing your shadow. I've always read that's something some people never liked...<br /> <br /> Love your idea of formor being an umbrella term.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue isn't so much Shadowguides, per se. It's just that it requires a lot of trust so people don't feel like there's antagonism at the table. It's the same as any degree of PvP, really. You need a good table and people who communicate to pull it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T14:00:59-07:00","id":1491238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HeavyWhiskey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1488988-speculation-on-future-5th-edition-content?p=1490193#post1490193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they <i>have</i> struck books from canon, at least once that I remember: The Red Death Trilogy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, McCann is reappearing in the epilogue of &quot;War in Heavens&quot; and Madlaine Giovanni mentions their past adventures, during that Trilogy.<br /> <br /> One could argue that &quot;War in Heavens&quot; was written/published before the decision to strike &quot;Red Death&quot; from canon was made, but still Madleine as a character reappears years later in the official comic of the clan (well, licensed product) and iirc also Rachel and Reuben from the Red Death trilogy. They are children of Seth, the third son of Adam and Eve, and should be Paradox magnets.... yet, they are in a licensed product...<br /> <br /> I'm not sure ever reading an official statement, what is canon in the game world and what is not. The Masquerade of the Red death books appeared on the official listing White Wolf release of all WoD publications, when the WoD ended. Back then, when the nWoD was about to be the only WoD.<br /> <br /> That said, the Gaki and Cats never made a come back in any book. KotE did create a complete retcon of what previously was written of the Far East (which was little). But, yes, there were actual shapeshifting beings that could take the form of everyone they once met, iirc, and they were cats, somehow. Never to be mentioned again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the events depicted in the Masquerade of the Red Death aren't so drastic, for the general vampire society, as that they needed to be retconned out of existence. They could have happened. I mean, what would really change if there was a few months in the 1990s in which a supernatural being killed vampires in Elysiums with fire?<br /> So, some Niktuku might have woken, or not, now difference to most games.<br /> So, there was a conclave in the Alpes, no difference for most games.<br /> So, there was a plot to diablerize Tremere/Saulot, no difference for most games, since it didn't succeed, anyway,<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}